id: pm-c3aiik
title: "GH-1325: history diff cursor drops newest rows and strands the final page"
description: "GitHub issue #1325 reproduces default-budget pm history <id> --diff --format json with a cursor that advances compact_history but not diff. Later pages repeat older diffs and can report has_more:true without next_cursor; close and release diffs become unreachable. Source: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1325"
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:history","area:output",defect,github
created_at: "2026-09-27T12:26:03.741Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-28T03:10:29.274Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#e953e6452c14bdf5bc2ec1d7"
author: "harness:codex"
acceptance_criteria: Reproduce with disposable 20-entry history and real tracker example; advance or independently continue all truncated diff rows; never emit has_more without a cursor; verify all rows and snapshot contracts with exact coverage
goal: project management = context management
objective: Every bounded history diff can be fully reconstructed through continuation cursors
value: Agents can recover the actual latest lifecycle and audit changes
impact: Prevent false conclusions that an item was never closed or released
outcome: Diff and compact history advance consistently and final pages have truthful continuation receipts
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: high
severity: high
repro_steps: Page pm history <id> --diff --format json with default budget using --output-cursor; diff repeats earlier indices and the final page has has_more without next_cursor.
affected_version: 2026.9.27
component: history output budgets and continuation
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-tqel,discovered_from,"2026-09-27T12:26:03.741Z","harness:codex","cli:create:dep",detected
comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-27T12:26:03.741Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: all-status GH-1325 and cursor-diff searches found the general output-budget feature pm-5t33or and closed history grammar work pm-tqel; neither owns this specific paired-diff continuation failure."
  "2026-09-27T23:32:22.717Z","harness:codex","Verification: linked diff continuation suite 3/3 passed and recorded test history. Manual isolated tracker replay covered more than 20 history events, independent diff cursors, exact row reconstruction, final-page termination, and explicit larger-budget recovery for an oversized individual diff. Full coverage passed 9380 tests at 100/100/100/100. Hosted review remains pending."
  "2026-09-27T23:57:41.258Z","harness:codex","PR #1332 review recurrence: Greptile P1 identified that history string-only budget compaction overwrote explicit output-limit has_more when no budget cursor existed. Preserved the explicit applied_bound signal and added a regression requiring strings_compacted=true, rows_compacted=false, no next_cursor, has_more=true. Linked four-test suite passed; full coverage pending."
  "2026-09-28T00:38:10.409Z","harness:codex","Review verification: focused history continuation suite 4/4 passed after the complexity-safe expression. Full static quality pipeline passed, including repository assurance, 100% docstring coverage, zero jscpd clones, and mutation gate. A full coverage run before the expression-only simplification passed 9381 tests at 100/100/100/100; final rerun hit two unrelated 30-second suite-load timeouts, and both timed-out tests passed in isolation. Hosted coverage shards will give the exact final-head result."
  "2026-09-28T01:30:14.076Z","harness:codex","PR #1332 second review: added diff-only history sentinel so row_contract exposes diff, and narrowed lossless string preservation to the diff collection while other history strings still compact. Focused 6-test continuation suite, typecheck, docs links, direct static-quality/docstring gate, and full 9383-test exact 100/100/100/100 coverage passed. Full static pipeline reached transport-floor check, which failed on host-sensitive latency (next 757>440 ms, create 651>398 ms, claim 598>415 ms); no threshold changed, hosted static pending."
  "2026-09-28T01:53:18.626Z","harness:codex","Review reproduction: PR #1332 Greptile thread PRRT_kwDORSgRDc6mglEX found two 2-row collections limited to one each return count=2 even though projection.row_key=history. Added failing regression (actual 2, expected 1) before the SDK fix; active projection row count is now used when present."
  "2026-09-28T02:18:53.293Z","harness:codex","Verification at branch ca3d4d788 plus working changes: focused regression 7/7 passed after a deliberately failing 2-versus-1 count assertion; full suite 9384 passed, two Windows-only skipped locally, exact V8 100/100/100/100 (65748 statements, 50308 branches, 13604 functions, 62794 lines). Static pipeline reached only a host-sensitive list transport floor 423>419 ms; isolated transport rerun passed all six operations, and graph-composition, record-integrity and mutation gates each passed. Hosted final-head check remains pending."
  "2026-09-28T03:10:29.274Z","harness:codex","Second CodeRabbit review round: corrected learning 1 through pm, rebuilt cursor row_contract for the selected diff collection, and protected only nested diff values from budget truncation. The stale-contract and empty-diff nested-history assertions both failed before their fixes; linked focused suite passed 8/8. Full suite passed 9385 tests with exact 100/100/100/100 V8 coverage (65751 statements, 50312 branches, 13604 functions, 62797 lines). Full quality:static, tag-aware changelog check, and defect-evidence gate passed. Final hosted head for these latest source changes remains pending."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-27T21:41:17.451Z","harness:codex",Temporary tracker with 20+ history entries showed compact_history and diff need independent cursors. Following a diff cursor now projects only diff and its own count. Oversized single rows require a larger output budget rather than silently shortened values.
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text,edited_at}:
  "2026-09-27T21:41:19.285Z","harness:codex",History continuation fingerprints must be computed from unmodified source rows. Deep-copy output before compaction and keep diff strings lossless. Cursor-based budget truncation needs a usable continuation cursor when has_more is true; explicit --output-limit may report has_more without next_cursor because callers can raise the row limit.,"2026-09-28T02:31:53.092Z"
